## Fixed: worker xray-data-3x7nj, PR #10302 (the commit tagged rf2-3x7nj.26.2)

**Reproduced at trunk 6b787c338b** (JVM probe against pinned Editscript 0.6.5). All five of the bead's shapes misprojected exactly as described:

- `[:todos 2 :done?]` read `:added`;
- `[0 :n]` read `:before 10`;
- `[2 :c]` read `:before ::missing`;
- `[:rows 2 1]` read `:added`;
- the set under a shift stayed one whole-set `:modified`.

The controls (no shift; the rf2-96csq4 index-leaf case) were correct. There was one further instance of the same class, and it is fixed too: a vector nested under a shifted element replayed against the wrong before counterpart, so its removals were dropped. For `{:rows [[1 2] [3 4 5]]} -> {:rows [[0 0] [1 2] [3 5]]}`, the removal of 4 was lost.

**Fix.** `translate-before-path` maps every integer segment of an after-coordinate path through its prefix vector's replay `:slots`, from the root down. It returns nil through an inserted element. Every before-side read uses it:

- the `:r` before value;
- a nested `:-` removed value;
- the `expand-collection-replacement` before value (from the raw script's own replays, which are exact for it because expansion only adds edits beneath a replaced path);
- each nested vector's replay length, via shallowest-first replays;
- the removals channel.

`mark-wholly-changed` runs both walks in AFTER coordinates:

- the `:added` walk pairs after-child i with before-element `slots[i]`;
- the `:removed` walk maps before-child j through an `:inverse` map and skips removed elements.

Spec 004 states the rule.

**Control.** There are seven regressions beside the rf2-96csq4 tests.

- Translation disabled: all seven go red, along with the rf2-96csq4 siblings.
- Last-segment-only translation (the pre-fix rule): the four nested-path tests go red.
- Equal-index pairing in the wholly-walk: the swapped-set-after-prepend pairing test goes red.

Each restore was verified by blob hash against the committed object. JVM tools/xray suite green.
Merged-PR audit #10302 (64b149cbe9edb965c3a60d681ef356465f8434bd; merged 2026-09-23T20:03:47Z). Completeness: All four claims implemented: epoch re-seeds and previews use the privacy gate; nested vector before paths are translated; map uniformity uses key union; same-kind whole replacements expand recursively. Correctness: Reviewed reducers and diff pipeline including shallowest-first replays, inserted slots, inverse pairing, descending removal tails and type-change controls. Accepted reported JVM 1392/6790, focused engine 96/460 and full node 12550/63274 results and specific negative controls; CI 37 successful checks. Implementation quality: Centralizes replay translation and replacement expansion instead of adding panel-specific exceptions. Tests pin public projection semantics independently of Editscript cost choices. No material additional finding. Actionable findings: none. Existing finding updates: none.

